# 25 October 2026 23:59: SEMANTIC EDITING. The third storey above parametric (the recipe's raw numbers) and procedural
# (the renderer): a reproduced sound is split into a few NAMED components (click, ring, thump, tail...), each with a
# short panel of sliders that mean something to the ear. One slider drives hundreds of raw numbers coherently.
#
# Exactness: the noise of every component is cut from the SAME noise draw by amplitude masks that sum to one, and the
# partials are shared out, so with every slider at its default the sum of the components IS the recipe's render
# (checked by Scripts/CheckSemantic.py). Every move is measured against the untouched sound in JND units.
# FR : édition sémantique. Composants nommés, curseurs qui ont un sens, identité exacte aux valeurs par défaut.
